kgsl: Add direct-MMIO SMMU aperture/HSR path for no-TZ OP-TEE boards

On OP-TEE+KVM boards like Shikra there is no TZ/QTEE to service the
SMMU aperture and BCL/tsense SCM calls, so per-process pagetables and
related SCM-backed register programming cannot go through the
existing qcom_scm_*/qtee_shmbridge_* path.

Detect this at probe time from the absence of a zap-shader
devicetree node and, when set, reprogram the SMMU aperture (S1CB0/
S1CB1/CTL).
 
Signed-off-by: Lokesh Kumar <lok@qti.qualcomm.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending
